# DTF tier manifest: rest-mutation-authz-1-11
#   (GHSA-mvmh-g8wm-r3cp / artifact-keeper#4588, artifact-keeper#4193 / #4200)
# Profile-set: filesystem + imagebuild.non-admin. Every gate under test sits in
# a REST handler ahead of storage, so the storage dimension is irrelevant.
# imagebuild.non-admin turns AK_IMAGE_BUILD_ADMIN_ONLY off, the non-default
# posture the advisory's image-build finding needs. No BuildKit is configured.
#
# THE BUGS (both fixed in 1.11.0; RED on 1.10.0)
#   #4193   PUT/POST/DELETE /api/v1/artifacts/{id}/labels[/{key}] checked the
#           write:artifacts token scope (a session always passes) and read
#           visibility. Any signed-in user rewrote labels on a public repo's
#           artifacts; a read-only member did so on a private one.
#   GHSA-mvmh  eight REST mutation routes stopped at a gate that does not
#           authorize a session (token scope, the tenant gate, or bare authn):
#             PUT  /promotion/repositories/{key}/release-target   -> admin
#             POST /promotion/repositories/{key}/artifacts/{id}/reject -> promote
#             PUT/POST/DELETE /repositories/{key}/labels[/{k}]    -> write
#             GET/POST/DELETE /repositories/{key}/email-subscriptions -> admin
#             POST /repositories/{key}/image-builds[/render]      -> write
#             PUT /builds/{id}, POST /builds/{id}/artifacts       -> creator/admin
#             POST /peers/{id}/connections/probe                  -> admin
#             POST /repositories/{key}/security/proxy-scans/rescan -> write
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1). Exploit callers: N (no grant),
# R (`reader` on private Q), a non-creator on a build. Each exploit case is
# refused 403/404 AND a DB read shows nothing changed; on 1.10.0 each answers
# 2xx (or the handler's own 404 past the missing gate) and the DB shows the
# write. Controls hold on both images: a `developer` member writes artifact
# and repository labels, renders an image build and passes the rescan gate; a
# fine-grained repository admin creates and lists email subscriptions and
# links the release target; admin rejects and probes; the build's creator
# updates it; a reader still lists labels.
#
# KNOWN-RED (reported, never failed): a `repository-owner` ROLE member is
# refused 403 on email-subscriptions and release-target PUT on the fixed
# images, although the 1.11.0 CHANGELOG says repository-owner members are
# unaffected (require_repo_admin reads fine-grained grants only):
# artifact-keeper#4818.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: five logins and ~50 back-to-back authenticated
# calls; the base default (ON) would throttle them into 429s.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem imagebuild.non-admin"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
